<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarhunt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tarhun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarhunt, also called Tarhun, was the storm god of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> and other Anatolian peoples and one of the chief deities of the Hittite pantheon. The Hittite Empire profile explains that the Hittite king ruled as the earthly representative of the storm god rather than as a god himself. This created a more negotiated relationship between royal and priestly authority than existed under Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divine-kingship">divine kingship</a>.</p></div>
